      {
        "id": "u2-t2",
        "title": "Queria: the polite way to order",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "rule",
            "title": "Quero or queria?",
            "text": "Querer means to want. Quero (I want) is direct. In cafés and shops people say queria (I'd like): softer and more polite."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "querer, present",
            "head": [
              "Person",
              "querer"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "eu",
                "quero"
              ],
              [
                "tu",
                "queres"
              ],
              [
                "ele, ela, você",
                "quer"
              ],
              [
                "nós",
                "queremos"
              ],
              [
                "eles, elas, vocês",
                "querem"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "examples",
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "u2-g04",
                "pt": "Queria um chá, por favor.",
                "en": "I'd like a tea, please."
              },
              {
                "id": "u2-g05",
                "pt": "Queres um café?",
                "en": "Do you want a coffee? (to a friend)"
              },
              {
                "id": "u2-g06",
                "pt": "Nós queremos dois galões.",
                "en": "We want two galões."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tip",
            "text": "Staff offer things with quer: Quer açúcar? Quer saco? Answer with Pode ser (sure) or Não, obrigado."
          }
